  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Vitamin D deficiency affects an estimated 40% of U.S. adults and a significantly
    higher proportion of men in northern latitudes or predominantly indoor occupations.
    It functions as a steroid hormone regulating immune response, testosterone synthesis,
    bone mineral density, mood, and cellular proliferation. Running deficient across all
    of those functions simultaneously is not a minor problem.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Mitigate pillar includes a targeted vitamin D testing and repletion protocol.
    This is one of the highest-yield, lowest-risk interventions in the entire 4M framework
    — and one of the most consistently neglected.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>25-OH Vitamin D Test</h3>
      <p>A simple blood test. Target optimal range 60–80 ng/mL, not just "normal" (which starts at 30).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Repletion Protocol</h3>
      <p>Dose-to-level, not dose-to-label. Most deficient adults need 5,000–10,000 IU/day with K2 for months to reach optimal.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Sunlight as Primary Source</h3>
      <p>20–30 minutes of midday sun on large skin areas is the physiologically preferred path when your latitude allows it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Co-Factors</h3>
      <p>Magnesium, vitamin K2, and boron support vitamin D conversion and utilization — the whole ecosystem matters.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

